cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "mip-heuristics"
type: software
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: Spoorendonk
    given-names: Simon
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4304-6956"
    email: simon@flowty.ai
abstract: "A unified open-source reference implementation and empirical evaluation of four modern primal heuristics for mixed-integer programming — FeasibilityJump, Fix-Propagate-Repair, LocalMIP and Scylla — integrated into the HiGHS solver behind a common interface with shared effort budgeting and solution submission, so they can be measured under identical conditions. Includes an LP-guided FPR variant dispatched during the branch-and-bound dive, continuous (opportunistic) parallel workers, and an end-to-end evaluation on the PLATO mipfeas benchmark. The combined configuration yields only a small aggregate improvement over vanilla HiGHS: the contribution is the open implementations, the common integration infrastructure and the comparable measurements, not a faster solver configuration."
